config INTC_EIOINTC
	bool "Loongson EIOINTC (extended I/O interrupt controller)"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_LOONGSON_LS2K0300_EIOINTC_ENABLED
	select LOONGARCH
	help
	  Enable the driver for the Loongson EIOINTC (extended I/O interrupt
	  controller, "EXTIOI" on the 2K0300). The controller provides up to 128
	  independent peripheral interrupt vectors and forwards them to a single
	  LoongArch CPU interrupt line.

	  It is the successor of the LIOINTC, which aggregates 32 peripheral
	  lines onto one CPU line, several of which the SoC wires to a group of
	  peripherals (uart2..uart5 share one line on the 2K0300). With the
	  static ISR table of this port only one handler can serve such a line,
	  so peripherals that need their own interrupt should use the EIOINTC.
